# API

One turn is one synchronous request: audio in, interviewer text and audio out.

Routes stay `GET /api/health`, `POST /api/sessions`, `POST /api/sessions/{id}/turns`, `POST /api/sessions/{id}/end`.

- Model ids, `VERBATIM`, language, and voice live in `api/settings.py`.
- `transcribe_audio` gets no system instruction. Dialogue uses `prompts/entrevistador.txt`. Feedback uses `prompts/feedback.txt` and runs only on end.
- Clear the uploaded audio after transcription. Session text stays in the process dict and is dropped on end.
- Keep FastAPI and `google-genai`. Do not add a package, a database, a websocket, or a second provider.
- Tests use `unittest` and mock Gemini.

```python
transcript = gemini_client.transcribe_audio(audio_bytes, mime_type)
audio_bytes = b""
```
